# The build context is the app directory. On a Home Assistant server the
# repository is freshly cloned so most of this is absent, but a local
# `docker build` would otherwise copy a developer's virtualenv, node_modules
# and previous build output straight into the image.

# Python
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov/

# Node — dependencies are installed inside the build, and dist is produced there
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# Local data: never copy a database or a secrets file into an image
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/secrets.json
**/secret.key

# Not needed at runtime
**/.git/
**/.DS_Store
